{
  "id": "ep224",
  "duration": 50.862,
  "beats": [
    {
      "start": 0.08,
      "end": 3.688,
      "text": "Black holes usually kill stars, but this one births them.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Anatomy of a Black Hole.jpg",
        "credit": "European Southern Observatory - ESO",
        "license": "CC BY 4.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Anatomy_of_a_Black_Hole.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 1.333,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 1.333,
          "end": 3.7,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 3.688,
      "end": 9.558,
      "text": "Most supermassive black holes act as thermostats, heating gas to prevent star formation.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Galaxy cluster IDCS J1426.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA, ESA, and M. Brodwin (University of Missouri)",
        "license": "CC BY 4.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Galaxy_cluster_IDCS_J1426.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 3.7,
          "end": 5.8,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 5.8,
          "end": 9.567,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 9.558,
      "end": 15.653,
      "text": "But the Phoenix Cluster, discovered in 2010, is a rule-breaking monster in the southern sky.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "South Pole Telescope (Pano3-2017Aug14-South-Pole-360-DrMichalik-CC3).jpg",
        "credit": "NOIRLab/NSF/AURA",
        "license": "CC BY 4.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:South_Pole_Telescope_(Pano3-2017Aug14-South-Pole-360-DrMichalik-CC3).jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 9.567,
          "end": 12.967,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 12.967,
          "end": 15.667,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 15.653,
      "end": 21.953,
      "text": "It generates more than seven hundred stars every year, shattering X-ray and star-birth records.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "SPT-CLJ2344\u20134243 (Phoenix Cluster) Chandra.jpg",
        "credit": "X-ray: NASA/CXC/MIT/M.McDonald et al; Optical: NASA/STScI",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:SPT-CLJ2344%E2%80%934243_(Phoenix_Cluster)_Chandra.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 15.667,
          "end": 18.8,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 18.8,
          "end": 21.967,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 21.953,
      "end": 26.298,
      "text": "Our Milky Way forms only one or two stars in that same time.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "ESO - Milky Way.jpg",
        "credit": "ESO/S. Brunier",
        "license": "CC BY 4.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:ESO_-_Milky_Way.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 21.967,
          "end": 23.9,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 23.9,
          "end": 26.3,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 26.298,
      "end": 32.293,
      "text": "Chandra and Hubble found cavities and filaments, while Webb spotted the gas cooling between them.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Artist concept of JWST (50489833002 107cb9e661 o).jpg",
        "credit": "Adriana Manrique Gutierrez, NASA Animator",
        "license": "CC BY 4.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Artist_concept_of_JWST_(50489833002_107cb9e661_o).jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 26.3,
          "end": 29.3,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 29.3,
          "end": 32.3,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 32.293,
      "end": 39.313,
      "text": "Despite weighing ten billion Suns, this black hole fails to heat nearby gas, allowing stars to form.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Black hole (NASA).jpg",
        "credit": "NASA/D. Berry",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Black_hole_(NASA).jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 32.3,
          "end": 35.567,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 35.567,
          "end": 39.3,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 39.313,
      "end": 45.513,
      "text": "This frantic growth spurt is unsustainable and will likely end within a hundred million years.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Hubble Sees 'Comet Galaxy' Being Ripped Apart By Galaxy Cluster (2007-12-2077).tiff",
        "credit": "NASA, ESA, and J. -P. Kneib (Laboratorie d'Astrophysique de Marseille)",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hubble_Sees_%27Comet_Galaxy%27_Being_Ripped_Apart_By_Galaxy_Cluster_(2007-12-2077).tiff"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 39.3,
          "end": 45.5,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 45.513,
      "end": 50.512,
      "text": "This makes the Phoenix Cluster a rare exception, as black holes usually kill stars.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Anatomy of a Black Hole.jpg",
        "credit": "European Southern Observatory - ESO",
        "license": "CC BY 4.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Anatomy_of_a_Black_Hole.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 45.5,
          "end": 50.867,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
